    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I check the user’s guide, but there’s no mention of an off button or power switch. On the Friend website, another chatbo",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 20982
        },
        {
          "text": "I think you just have to unpair it from the app or maybe just let the battery run down if you really want it totally dar",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 21183
        }
      ],
      "words": 63
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "She asks Chat for support. Always compliant, it says: “You are not only doing your job; you are doing it well.” And if t",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 23988
        }
      ],
      "words": 34
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Arendt observed that when people don’t feel part of a community, they panic and look for reassurance. They seek simplici",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 25012
        },
        {
          "text": "is the fact that loneliness, once a borderline experience",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 25251
        },
        {
          "text": "has become an everyday experience.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 25310
        }
      ],
      "words": 49
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But for Luke, what worked for previous generations seems out of range. He doesn’t even try to start that real club",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 28434
        },
        {
          "text": "It’s easier to talk to Chat, who always tells him things will work out",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 28633
        }
      ],
      "words": 36
    },
    {
      "block": "原句13",
      "no": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I answer him not with a philosophical argument, but by telling him the story of how three people in that room had prayed",
          "ok": true,
